

### 1\. Create students

```cypher
CREATE
(s1:Student {id: 101, name: "Srushti", age: 20}),
(s2:Student {id: 102, name: "Archita", age: 21}),
(s3:Student {id: 103, name: "Anjali", age: 19}),
(s4:Student {id: 104, name: "Manali", age: 22}),
(s5:Student {id: 105, name: "Aditi", age: 20});
```

### 2\. Create subjects

```cypher
CREATE
(s1:Subject {id: 201, name: "CSL", courseCode: "CSL101"}),
(s2:Subject {id: 202, name: "NLP", courseCode: "NLP201"}),
(s3:Subject {id: 203, name: "ML", courseCode: "ML301"}),
(s4:Subject {id: 204, name: "ARVR", courseCode: "ARVR401"}),
(s5:Subject {id: 205, name: "BDA", courseCode: "BDA501"});
```

### 3\. Display nodes

```cypher
MATCH (n:Student)
RETURN n;
```

```cypher
MATCH (n:Subject)
RETURN n;
```

### 4\. Create relationships

```cypher
MATCH
(s1:Student {name: "Srushti"}),
(s2:Student {name: "Archita"}),
(s3:Student {name: "Anjali"}),
(s4:Student {name: "Manali"}),
(s5:Student {name: "Aditi"}),
(t1:Subject {name: "CSL"}),
(t2:Subject {name: "NLP"}),
(t3:Subject {name: "ML"}),
(t4:Subject {name: "ARVR"}),
(t5:Subject {name: "BDA"})
CREATE
(s1)-[:ENROLLED_IN]->(t1),
(s2)-[:ENROLLED_IN]->(t2),
(s3)-[:ENROLLED_IN]->(t3),
(s4)-[:ENROLLED_IN]->(t4),
(s5)-[:ENROLLED_IN]->(t5);
```

### 5\. Update Archita's age

```cypher
MATCH (s:Student {name: "Archita"})
SET s.age = 22
RETURN s;
```

### 6\. Display relationships

```cypher
MATCH p=()-[:ENROLLED_IN]->()
RETURN p;
```

### 7\. Delete Manali

```cypher
MATCH (s:Student {name: "Manali"})
DETACH DELETE s;
```

### 8\. Display final graph

```cypher
MATCH (n)
RETURN n;
```

Meanings to remember

| Command          | Meaning                              |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| CREATE           | Creates nodes or relationships       |
| MATCH            | Finds nodes or graph patterns        |
| SET              | Adds or updates a property           |
| RETURN           | Displays results                     |
| DETACH DELETE    | Deletes a node and its relationships |
| ENROLLED_IN      | Relationship type                    |
| Student, Subject | Node labels                          |
| name, age, id    | Properties                           |
| ()               | Node pattern                         |
| []               | Relationship pattern                 |
| ->               | Relationship direction               |